feat(memory): auto-capture in the REAL turn loop (Self-Gardening goes live)

Auto-capture was test-panel-only; now it fires on ACTUAL conversation.

- agent_stream (Anthropic path): after the turn completes + checkpoints,
  run memory::auto_capture over the USER's prompt (the human's input carries
  the durable facts). Fully best-effort: gated on a per-agent toggle, runs
  only with a vault scope, resolves Memory/ THROUGH THE JAIL BROKER, swallows
  errors, never blocks/breaks the reply. Emits a small "remembered N new,
  reinforced M" info event when it captures something.
- db migration 7: agent_settings.auto_remember (default 1 = ON; capture is
  salience+novelty gated so it's conservative + safe). ALTER ADD, forward-only.
- repo: get_auto_remember / set_auto_remember (default ON when absent).
- lib.rs: memory_auto_remember_enabled gate + memory_get/set_auto_remember
  cmds so the UI can toggle per agent.

Now a normal chat ("I prefer dark roast; I decided to ship at $20") quietly
deposits L2 atoms into the vault, novelty-deduped, no button. The loop the
whole memory arc was built for, firing on real use.
